# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOY-TIME configuration for deploy/deploy.ps1
#
# Copy this file to deploy/.env and fill it in. deploy/.env is gitignored.
#
# These three values say WHERE to deploy and WHAT PROVES you may. They are the
# only keys this file accepts: deploy.ps1 refuses to run if it finds anything
# else here, precisely so that a runtime secret pasted in by mistake is caught
# instead of being shipped inside the deployment package.
#
# RUNTIME configuration - APP_ENV, APP_SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL, CORS_ORIGINS,
# DEFAULT_LOCALE and the auth cookie settings - belongs in the CapRover app's
# own environment variables, NOT here and NOT in the tarball.
# See docs/04_technical/ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CapRover dashboard URL, e.g. https://captain.example.com
CAPROVER_URL=https://captain.example.com

# Name of the CapRover application to deploy into.
CAPROVER_APP=handbase-web

# App-scoped deploy token, from the CapRover dashboard:
#   Apps -> <your app> -> Deployment -> "App Token"
#
# Scoped to this one application, so it cannot administer the CapRover server
# the way the account password can. Leave it empty here and export
# CAPROVER_APP_TOKEN in the shell instead if you would rather not have it on
# disk at all - deploy.ps1 falls back to the environment for every key.
CAPROVER_APP_TOKEN=
